## 9 The kernels and the host

PSK-Kernel is the loop nests the backends run: one kernel per distinct nest, under its type and its layout. The host program launches them, converting a value where a kernel reads it in another type.

```text
-- 4 kernels, 5 launches, f32
-- fusion: 10 launches without it, 5 saved (50%)
```

Each kernel under the sites that launch it, as the host recorded them:

```text
// k0: 2 launches at LayerNorm.apply/%3 (μ), LayerNorm.apply/%6 (σ2)
kernel mean axis model (%0 : f32[batch: 3, model: 8]) -> %1 : f32[batch: 3] {
  for i0 in 0..3 {
    s0 = 0
    for i1 in 0..8 {
      s0 = (s0 + %0[i0, i1])
    }
    %1[i0] = (s0 / 8)
  }
}
// k1: 1 launch at LayerNorm.apply/%5 (fused)
kernel fused 2 steps (%0 : f32[batch: 3, model: 8], %1 : f32[batch: 3]) -> %2 : f32[batch: 3, model: 8] {
  for i0 in 0..3 {
    for i1 in 0..8 {
      %2[i0, i1] = ((%0[i0, i1] - %1[i0]) * (%0[i0, i1] - %1[i0]))
    }
  }
}
// k2: 1 launch at LayerNorm.apply/%10 (fused)
kernel fused 2 steps (%0 : f32[batch: 3], %1 : f32[]) -> %2 : f32[batch: 3] {
  for i0 in 0..3 {
    %2[i0] = sqrt((%0[i0] + %1[]))
  }
}
// k3: 1 launch at LayerNorm.apply/%15 (fused)
kernel fused 4 steps (%0 : f32[batch: 3, model: 8], %1 : f32[batch: 3], %2 : f32[batch: 3], %3 : f32[8], %4 : f32[8]) -> %5 : f32[batch: 3, model: 8] {
  for i0 in 0..3 {
    for i1 in 0..8 {
      %5[i0, i1] = ((((%0[i0, i1] - %1[i0]) / %2[i0]) * %3[i1]) + %4[i1])
    }
  }
}
```

**The host**, as the C export prints it (§10): a function per Presk function, a fold a loop, each launch under the site it computes and each conversion where a kernel reads a value in another type.

```c
void presk_LayerNorm_8_apply(presk_arena *arena, const presk_LayerNorm_8_apply_in *in, presk_LayerNorm_8_apply_out *out)
{
    const float *theta_gamma = in->theta_gamma;
    const float *theta_beta = in->theta_beta;
    const float *x = in->x;
    float *result = presk_alloc(arena, 24 * sizeof(float));
    const size_t mark = presk_mark(arena);
    /* LayerNorm.apply/%3 (μ) */
    float *mu = presk_alloc(arena, 3 * sizeof(float));
    k0(x, mu, 0, 3);
    /* LayerNorm.apply/%5 (fused) */
    float *t5 = presk_alloc(arena, 24 * sizeof(float));
    k1(x, mu, t5, 0, 3);
    /* LayerNorm.apply/%6 (σ2) */
    float *sigma2 = presk_alloc(arena, 3 * sizeof(float));
    k0(t5, sigma2, 0, 3);
    /* LayerNorm.apply/%8 */
    float *t8 = presk_alloc(arena, 1 * sizeof(float));
    presk_fill(t8, PRESK_F32, in->eps, 1);
    /* LayerNorm.apply/%10 (fused) */
    float *t10 = presk_alloc(arena, 3 * sizeof(float));
    k2(sigma2, t8, t10, 0, 3);
    /* LayerNorm.apply/%15 (fused) */
    k3(x, mu, t10, theta_gamma, theta_beta, result, 0, 3);
    out->result = result;
    presk_release(arena, mark);
}
```

*Command:* `presk dump ../../tests/examples/layernorm/layernorm.psk --stage kernel --entry LayerNorm{8}.apply --dim batch=3 --plan @$DOC/artifacts/plan.json`

## 10 Targets

**Native.** The Cranelift backend compiles each of the 4 kernels to machine code at its first launch, in process, and the host program of §9 runs them.

## 11 Measured

What one run measured on this machine: the realization natively against the exact reference, a call timed, each kernel's time beside the model's prediction, and the host's time by phase. The one section that changes from run to run.

Not measured: `--measure` was not given. Every other section is deterministic; this one would hold times.

## 12 Sites through every stage

A site is named `<function>/%<n>` at every stage, which is what lets one value be followed from PSK-Core to the C.

By default, the three largest shares of the solver's estimate (the three largest bounds without a solve), then the three nests of the most predicted time a call; `--site` names others.

**`LayerNorm.apply/%5`**

| Stage |  |
|---------------|------------------------------------|
| PSK-Core (§3) | `%5 : ℝ[..., model: D] = pow 2 %4` in `LayerNorm.apply` |
| Envelope (§6.1) | \|v\| ≤ 4.941e0, 24 elements |
| Type (§6.3) | `f32`, decision |
| Fusion (§7) | ends a group of 2: read by `σ2 : ℝ[...] = mean axis model %5`: a reduction |
| Layout (§8) | nest `LayerNorm.apply/%5`, 5 points at `[3, 8] [3]`; chosen lanes 1, split none, 0.0128 µs, bound by work; runner-up lanes 1, split (0, 5), 101.5 µs |
| Kernel (§9) | `k1`: `kernel fused 2 steps (%0 : f32[batch: 3, model: 8], %1 : f32[batch: 3]) -> %2 : f32[batch: 3, model: 8]` |

**`LayerNorm.apply/%15`**

| Stage |  |
|---------------|------------------------------------|
| PSK-Core (§3) | `%15 : ℝ[..., model: D] = add %13, β` in `LayerNorm.apply` |
| Envelope (§6.1) | \|v\| ≤ 2.125e0, 24 elements |
| Type (§6.3) | `f32`, decision |
| Fusion (§7) | ends a group of 4: the function's result |
